{"p":"pex","e":"pex","x":{"texts":["DESCRIPTION:","pex:pex events complete the base Permanent Events (with eXtra) (null)data protocol","{pex:<EventJson>} is detected as {p:pex e:pex x:<EventJson>} (note here pex/x MUST be a json)","up to this point all detected data per opreturn output MUST be a complete valid json parse","BUT pex:pex events can also be detected by joining strings, as long as the same _marginal_ address is used","an EventJson can be split into multiple opreturn outputs in one or more transactions","DETECTION:","the opreturn outputs are linked by reusing the same address in the first input AND the first output, which is called a marginal address","the final opreturn output links to the beginning, and completes a valid json","an opreturn output string that starts with the characters pex_<countNumber>:{ begins the json","countNumber is the total opreturn outputs, by the same marginal address, which all joined will complete an EventJson","the following opreturn outputs after the first use the format pex[<reverseCount>]:<partOfAJson>, ending with pex_<idFirstOpreturnOutput>:<lastPartOfAJson>","the id for the joined pex event will be of the LAST opreturn output finalizing the json, which conveniently links to where it begins"],"bouts_escapedquotes":[{"987654x3x2":"pex_4:{\"tex"},{"987655x60x12":"pex[3]:ts\":"},{"987656x900x8":"pex[2]:[\"a\","},{"987657x65x4":"pex_987654x3x2:\"b\"]}"}],"pex_equivalent_from_split_bouts":{"987657x65x4":{"pex":{"texts":["a","b"]}}}}}